title: Hinges and turning contraptions
intro: Hinge joints pin a body to the world or to another body at a point, with limits on how far it swings and a motor to turn it; and welded contraptions turn as one body.
project: Contraption | Hinges

# A new scene in the Contraption project (which has a wheel picture, Textures/wheel.png), its camera moved out to see it
# all: a floor 40 wide whose top is at y = -2.5.
menu: File > New Scene...
prompt: Hinges
select: Main Camera
set: Transform.Position = 0, 1, 0
set: Camera.Size = 7
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Floor
set: Transform.Position = 0, -3, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 40, 1
set: Sprite.Tint = #4A4E5A
add: BoxCollider
set: BoxCollider.Size = 40, 1
deselect

chapter: A door | Its hinge and limits dragged in the Scene view
create: Sprite
rename: Door
set: Transform.Position = 4, 2, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 3, 0.3
set: Sprite.Tint = #B07F4A
add: BoxCollider
set: BoxCollider.Size = 3, 0.3
menu: Entity > Add Hinge
expectcomponents: Door = Transform, Sprite, BoxCollider, Body, HingeJoint
expectvalue: Door.Body.Rotates = true
say: Add Hinge pins the selection at its middle so it turns there, and makes its body rotate.
explain: handle:HingeJoint.Anchor | The hinge | Drag its knob to move it: here, to the door's left end.
path: HingeJoint.Anchor = -1.5, 0
expectvalue: Door.HingeJoint.Anchor.X = -1.5 ~ 0.01
set: HingeJoint.Limit = true
explain: handle:HingeJoint.Lower | Its limits | With Limit ticked, the wedge shows how far it swings: drag either end to set that limit.
path: HingeJoint.Lower = -60
expectvalue: Door.HingeJoint.LowerAngle = -60 ~ 1
path: HingeJoint.Upper = 20
expectvalue: Door.HingeJoint.UpperAngle = 20 ~ 1
deselect

chapter: A cart | Wheels hinged to it, turned by motors
create: Sprite
rename: Cart
set: Transform.Position = -6, -1.6, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 3, 0.4
set: Sprite.Tint = #B07F4A
add: BoxCollider
set: BoxCollider.Size = 3, 0.4
add: Body
set: Body.Rotates = true
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Back Wheel
set: Transform.Position = -7, -2.05, 0
pickimage: Sprite.Image = Textures/wheel.png
set: Sprite.Size = 0.9, 0.9
add: CircleCollider
set: CircleCollider.Radius = 0.45
select: Cart
select: Ctrl+Back Wheel
menu: Entity > Add Hinge
expectvalue: Back Wheel.HingeJoint.To = Cart
say: With two picked, the last is hinged to the first: this wheel turns on the cart, and the two don't bump into each other.
select: Ctrl+Cart
set: HingeJoint.Motor = true
set: HingeJoint.MotorSpeed = -360
explain: component:HingeJoint | A motor | Its motor turns it at its speed, as hard as its strength lets it. A wire into its Power switches it on and off.
menu: Entity > Duplicate
rename: Front Wheel
set: Transform.Position = -5, -2.05, 0
deselect

chapter: Turning as one | A welded contraption tips over
create: Sprite
rename: Post
set: Transform.Position = -1, -1.5, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 0.4, 2
set: Sprite.Tint = #4A4E5A
add: BoxCollider
set: BoxCollider.Size = 0.4, 2
deselect
create: Crate
rename: Box
set: Transform.Position = -0.2, 0.3, 0
set: Body.Rotates = true
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Beam
set: Transform.Position = -0.2, -0.35, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 2.4, 0.3
set: Sprite.Tint = #8C93A0
add: BoxCollider
set: BoxCollider.Size = 2.4, 0.3
add: Body
set: Body.Rotates = true
add: Weld
set: Weld.To = Box
say: Welded together, a beam and a box are one body now, which turns round where its weight balances: just off this post.
deselect

play
wait: 4
expectvalue: Door.Body.Asleep = true
explain: entity:Door | Swung down | The door swung down on its hinge as far as its lower limit, and fell asleep there.
explain: entity:Cart | Driving | The wheels' motors drive the cart along.
expectvalue: Beam.Body.Asleep = true
explain: entity:Beam | Tipped over | The welded beam and box tipped off the post together and lie on the floor as one.
stop
